  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(a)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>Ce</mi><mprescripts/><mn>58</mn><none/></mmultiscripts><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>Xe</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>In complex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>Xe</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup></math></p><p>there is no unpaired electron so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>(b)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mmultiscripts><mi>Gd</mi><mprescripts/><mn>64</mn><none/></mmultiscripts><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>Xe</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup></math></p><p>contain seven unpaired electrons so,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>63</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>(c)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mmultiscripts><mi>Eu</mi><mprescripts/><mn>63</mn><none/></mmultiscripts><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mmultiscripts><mi>Xe</mi><mprescripts/><mn>54</mn><none/></mmultiscripts></mfenced><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></math></p><p>contain six unpaired electron&nbsp;</p><p>so,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>6</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>48</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Hence, order of spin only magnetic movement&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math></p>"
